# AI service

- FastAPI in `services/ai`; **internal-only**: requires `X-Internal-Token` matching `AI_SERVICE_TOKEN`
- Env via `pydantic-settings`; fail fast on missing keys at boot
- Pydantic request/response models mirrored in `packages/contracts`
- All OpenAI calls use **Structured Outputs** (`response_format={"type":"json_schema", ...}`) — no freeform JSON parsing
- Model selection from env: `OPENAI_MODEL_EXTRACT` (default `gpt-4o`), `OPENAI_MODEL_RECOMMEND` (default `gpt-4o-mini`)
- Return per-field confidence (0..1) + `usage` (promptTokens, completionTokens, costUsdEstimate)
- Retry OpenAI calls with exponential backoff; timeout configurable
- PII guard: strip Luhn-valid PAN candidates from logs/breadcrumbs before persisting
- Sentry + `structlog` initialized; logs include requestId

## Endpoints

- `POST /extract`: image (multipart or signed URL) → preprocess → OpenAI Vision → structured JSON with `fieldConfidence`
- `POST /recommend`: pre-aggregated summary (NOT raw receipts) → recommendation list with `sourceReceiptIds`, `sourceSubscriptionId`, `confidence`
- `GET /health`: `{ok, model, promptVersions}`

## Image preprocessing (Pillow)

- HEIC → JPEG (`pillow-heif`)
- EXIF rotation applied
- Resize longest edge ≤ 2048px
- PDF: render first page to image
- JPEG quality 85 for cost control

## Testing

```bash
cd services/ai && pytest tests -q
```

- Mock OpenAI client; never call live API in CI
- Fixture-driven `/extract` tests:
  - `fixtures/receipts/*.jpg` + matching `*.json` ground truth
  - Assert merchant exact, total within ±$0.01, item count exact, all fields populated
- Contract tests: response schema matches `packages/contracts` TS types
- Internal-token tests: missing / wrong token → 401
